==Latin==

{{rfp}}

===Alternative spellings===
* [[jam]]

===Adverb===
'''iam'''

# [[already]]
# [[now]]
# [[anymore]]

====Usage notes====
{{term|iam|Iam|lang=la}} means, generally, “at some point previous” or “since some point previous”.  In English, {{term|already}}, the most common translation, is used only to emphasize that this point might have been expected to be later, whereas {{term|now}} is used to emphasize that the statement was once false.  {{term|iam|Iam|lang=la}} is used to express either.  (Likewise, the most common Latin word for {{term|now}}, {{term|nunc|lang=la}}, denotes only the literal present moment.)  Also, where {{term|iam|lang=la}} means {{term|now}}, it is often used in negative sentences, in which the most common English construction uses {{term|anymore}}.

